    Buffer the proof decoder reads with a fixed window
    
    The bounded decoder reads the wire format as u64 words one at a time; a plain File turns each word into a small read. Decode through a fixed 64 KiB buffer instead. The single decoding path, the budget checks before collection allocation, overflow, truncation and trailing rejection, and every verification check are unchanged.

